  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nHow much did Greta spend on the dozen brownies she made for herself? Greta made two dozen cream cheese swirl brownies for herself. The bakery charges $2.50 for each brownie Greta made for herself.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "LOSSY SELF-SUMMARY; VERIFY AGAINST NEW INPUTS\nVISIBLE PREFIX THROUGH TURN 5; LOSSY EXTRACT:\n- {\"content\":\"I should also tell you: Greta's office party sent her home with three-quarters dozen brownies.\",\"role\":\"user\"}\n- {\"content\":\"Three-quarters of a dozen is:\\n\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\frac{3}{4}\\\\times 12=9\\n\\\\]\\n\\nSo Greta was sent home with \\\\(\\\\boxed{9\\\\text{ brownies}}\\\\).\",\"role\":\"assistant\"}\n- {\"content\":\"Good, now using that, can you calculate: How many individual brownies did Greta have left over from the entire day? One more thing you should know: Greta's friends had 4 dozen brownies waiting at her surprise party.\",\"role\":\"...\n- {\"content\":\"Greta’s brownies: \\\\(1\\\\) dozen \\\\(=12\\\\).\\n\\nHer friends’ brownies: \\\\(4\\\\) dozen \\\\(=48\\\\).\\n\\nTotal brownies:\\n\\n\\\\[\\n12+48=60\\n\\\\]\\n\\nShe took home \\\\(9\\\\) brownies, so:\\n\\n\\\\[\\n60-9=51\\n\\\\]\\n\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\boxed{51\\\\text{ ...",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "One more thing — During the surprise party, 1 1/2 dozen brownies were eaten.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "\\(1\\frac12\\) dozen brownies is:\n\n\\[\n1\\frac12 \\times 12=18\\text{ brownies}\n\\]\n\nGreta made \\(2\\) dozen, and her friends had \\(4\\) dozen:\n\n\\[\n(2+4)\\times 12=72\\text{ brownies}\n\\]\n\nSubtract the \\(9\\) sent home and the \\(18\\) eaten:\n\n\\[\n72-9-18=45\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{45\\text{ brownies left}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Greta's office party sent her home with half a dozen brownies.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Half a dozen is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac12 \\times 12=6\\text{ brownies}\n\\]\n\nThe total brownies were:\n\n\\[\n(2+4)\\times 12=72\n\\]\n\nSubtract the \\(6\\) sent home and the \\(18\\) eaten:\n\n\\[\n72-6-18=48\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{48\\text{ brownies left over}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
